Hi managers,

Well I eventually gave up getting Hylafax 4.1.2 to compile with GCC, and 
got hold of a copy of CXX instead.

Courtesy of Bruce Young here's what you need to do:

Firstly fix the configure script. There are couple of places which refer 
to dec-osf-4 which need changing to dec-osf
The forthcoming 4.1.3 version of Hylafax should have this fixed - it has 
been in current CVS version.

Secondly: port.h has 3 prototypes that are not required after you have 
configured.  These need to be deleted.
Look in the port.h file and if present delete any prototypes for 
connect(), getsockopt(), setsockopt().

Out of interest, does anyone know why Compaq decided to drop Hylafax from 
the Open Source Software Collection ?


Regards,

Rob Leadbeater

