	Sys: Compaq Alpha DS10, Tru64 5.1 


I have read that:
uerf is no longer supported on newer machines like the ES45 
Instead use CompaqAnalyze (ca(8) which is part of WEBES 

I found an error on the console this morning and wanted to 
investigate more. I did `uerf -c err -o brief -R | more` and paged 
down a few times and uerf did: Segmentation fault (core dumped).

If I do`uerf -c oper -o brief -R | more` I get: 
Error reading syserr file.

I wasn't sure if my system should still be supporting uerf, does 
anyone know? 

I have also been getting a "S97evm: Communication with binlogd is 
not functioning" at boot time and was wondering if this is related? 

I had put this down to the fact that there wasn't a link in rc3.d to 
/sbin/init.d/binlog before the evm starts. binlogd wasn't running at all 
but I could write to the binary.errlog using logger -b testing.

I am tring to cut down on un-necessary processes but don't want to 
lose valuable system info. Should binlogd be running? 

