Deconstruct the logical units on the source HSG:

    =09DELETE unit-name
    =09DELETE storage-set-name
    =09DELETE device-name ...

    =09Move the disks and reconstruct the units on the target
    =09HSG:

    =09ADD DISK ...
    =09...
    =09ADD MIRROR ...
    =09ADD UNIT ...

    =09Be sure to skip the INIT step, since that WILL cause the
    =09data on those disks to disappear.

    =09TRANSPORTABLE is a characteristic supported by the HS
    =09family operating system that doesn't allocate space
    =09on the disk for the operating system's metadata.  The
    =09intent is to allow disks to be used on the HS family
    =09subsystem and then moved to a non-HS family subsystem
    =09such as a bare SCSI adapter.

    =09The HS family allocates some part of the space of a device
    =09for its metadata.  This is used to keep track of bad blocks,
    =09so that it can replace the block, but remember that the data
    =09in that block was wrong.  It also allows the feature of taking
    =09a bare disk, and turning it into a member of a mirror set.
    =09The data has lots of uses, but takes away some of the capacity
    =09that would be presented to the host.  TRANSPORTABLE doesn't
    =09allocate this space, with the attendent loss of features.
