Hi all,

My special thanks to Tony Patton who simulated the similar setup and =
pin-point the problem.
Also I 'm thankful to Patrick Miguel, Jeffrey Hummel, ROBIN Jean-Marie, =
Murtaza, Devesh Pant for giving guidance on the same topic.

Solution to the problem:

a) Sample of /etc/printcap file on Alphaserver:

lp2|dmp:\
      :lf=3D/usr/adm/lp*err:\
      :lp=3D:\
      :rm=3Dwin2k:\
      :rp=3Ddmp:\
      :sd=3D/usr/spool/lpd*:
=20
* is the extension file/ directory names.

win2k is Intel server name which we can ping from Alphaserver
dmp is the name of printer defined in windows2000. Local printing =
through Win2k works ok.

b) Configured "Print Services for Unix" on Windows2000 Server

c) After this start TCP/IP Print Service, which By default doesn't start =
automatically.

This solution really works!

Thanks again.
Regards.
Vimal Upreti

