all is fine during updating the os, but at the end I can't rebuild the kernel...
the message when trying to rebuild is:

*** WARNING ***
An error has occurred during system configuration.  A partial listing
of the error log file (/sys/BOHOR/errs) follows:

Make: Don't know how to make kern/lockinfo.c.  Stop.


In the documentation I read:

"Use setld command to removed le layered product that caused the failure..."

I don't known the product to be removed?

What is wrong in my kernel conf file BOHOR?

-----------------------------------------------------

thank you very much: Oisin McGuinness and Kalle Henk

thank you very much to Kalle Henk , He resolves my problem very fast!

his answer:


the problem is a known issue. Perform the following action and then build a 
kernel.
 
-cd /sys
- touch all the file in the following directories. kern , BINARY, ufs, data, 
net, bsd, io/*/* and conf
- doconfig -c <configfile>
 


I can build the kernel now!!!

